/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  packing02_schulz_0p02bar  --  a STRUCTURED-PACKING bed at total reflux, its HETP and
  pressure drop computed from the packing geometry (DEV.md 4c C329).

  THE TEST: Schulz, Rietfort, Jansen & Olujic, Chem. Eng. Trans. 69 (2018)
  763: FRI low-pressure column, 1.22 m, Montz-Pak A3-500M (corrugated wire
  gauze, 60 deg corrugations, installed area 478 m2/m3 measured on the
  delivered packing, void fraction ~0.92), bed 2.2 m (13 layers), p-xylene /
  o-xylene at total reflux, top pressure 0.02 bar.  HETP = bed height /
  Fenske stages between the distributor and the cross-sampler below the bed
  (section 2) -- the KPI `HETP` here is that definition.

  THE MODEL: Rocha, Bravo & Fair -- hydraulics (holdup, pressure drop,
  flooding at 1025 Pa/m), IECR 32 (1993) 641, Eqs 20-29; mass transfer,
  IECR 35 (1996) 1660, Eqs 5-17, the GAUZE effective area of Eq 14.  The
  composition is integrated up the bed, dy/dz = (y* - y)/H_OG; the pressure
  falls by the bed's own pressure drop from the bottom to the declared top.

  WHY NOT BILLET & SCHULTES 1999 (the folder holds it): its Table 2b gives
  constants for Montz B1-200, B2-300, C1-200, C2-200 and no gauze packing --
  nothing for A3-500M.  Rocha-Bravo-Fair needs only the geometry.

  MEASURED INPUTS (Schulz section 2 and Table 1): diameter, bed height,
    installed area 478, void fraction 0.92, angle 60 deg, top pressure; the
    liquid viscosity 0.539 mPa s (Table 1 -- the package has no
    liquid-viscosity record for the xylenes).
  ESTIMATED: the corrugation side S = 9 mm -- NOT in the paper ("with
    corrugation dimensions known", p. 765, but not printed); taken as Sulzer
    BX's, the gauze packing of the same area class (492 m2/m3, 60 deg) in
    Rocha-Bravo-Fair 1993 Table IV.  This is the one geometric number not
    from the source; HETP is roughly proportional to it.
  ASSUMED: the reboiler liquid 0.17 mol fraction p-xylene, chosen so that the
    bed's mean liquid is near Table 1's average composition (0.49);
    the vapour molar flow is taken constant up the bed.
  ESTIMATED PROPERTIES: as listed in constant/thermoPhysPropDict, plus
    Wilke-Chang liquid diffusivity and Rackett liquid density.
  FITTED: nothing (and nothing at 0.10 bar to carry over): this is a
    PREDICTION of the 0.02 bar curve.
  HELD-OUT: every point of Schulz Fig. 2b at 0.02 bar (DIGITISED from the
    figure, 180 ppi raster; method and uncertainty in
    docs/design/c329-ratebased-first-delivery.md).
  IN-SAMPLE OR NOT: the Rocha-Bravo-Fair 1996 data bank (Table 2) holds
    Sulzer BX with o-/p-xylenes at 0.021, 0.39 and 1.0 bar (Sakata 1972) --
    the same system and a gauze packing of the same class, not this packing
    and not these runs.  Out of sample for A3-500M; the system and the gauze
    area law are not new to the model.

  THE SWEEP moves the boil-up F-factor (reboiler vapour on the tower area)
  and stops below the model's hydraulic flood (F_G about 3.1 at both pressures).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        column;
        type        distillationColumn;
        model       totalReflux;

        operation
        {
            P              0.02 bar;      // TOP pressure
            condenser      { type total; }

            totalReflux
            {
                fFactor        1.5;      // swept; (m/s)(kg/m3)^0.5, reboiler vapour on the tower area
                specifiedAt    reboiler;
                composition
                {
                    pXylene    0.17;
                    oXylene    0.83;
                }
            }

            packing
            {
                model             RochaBravoFair;
                diameter          1.22 m;      // Schulz section 2
                height            2.2 m;       // Schulz section 2
                specificArea      478;         // m2/m3, installed (Schulz section 2)
                voidFraction      0.92;        // Schulz section 2 ("around 0.92")
                corrugationAngle  60;          // deg from the horizontal (Schulz section 2)
                corrugationSide   0.009 m;     // ESTIMATED: Sulzer BX (RBF 1993 Table IV)
                surface           gauze;       // RBF 1996 Eq 14
                lightKey          pXylene;
                liquidViscosity   5.39e-4;       // Pa s, Schulz Table 1
                segments          100;
            }
        }
    }
);
